<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cham sack of Angkor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1177</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cham">Cham</a> sack of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor">Angkor</a> occurred in 1177, when forces of the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a> captured and plundered the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer Empire</a>. The attack exposed the empire's vulnerabilities. It prompted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayavarman-vii">Jayavarman VII</a> to drive out the Cham, reorganise the military and fortify the new capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor-thom">Angkor Thom</a>.</p></div>
